     [38;5;246mContext fields are dropped unless explicitly declared loggable. Fails closed, so a newly added sensitive field [39m
     [38;5;246mnever lands in persisted logs by default.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Deny-list
     [38;5;246mScrub values under known-sensitive key patterns (password, token, secret). Low friction; fails open when a new [39m
     [38;5;246msensitive field name appears.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Call-site discipline only
     [38;5;246mNo redaction code; rely on reviewers to not log secrets. Zero machinery, no safety net once logs persist to disk.[39m
